  "description": "A parametric KITCHEN SINK on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nTHE HALF BOWL IS A DIVISOR, not a special case. Single, one-and-a-half and double are the same two-bowl construction with the split moved: the divider sits at 1/1, 1/1.6 or 1/2 of the bowl run, and Single simply drops the second bowl. That is one number changing, so a sink can be resized without any of the three arrangements breaking.\n\nTHE DRAINER TAKES ITS LENGTH FROM WHAT IS LEFT. Turn it on and the bowl run shrinks to 60% of the deck, so the two always add up to the sink you asked for rather than overflowing it. Turn it off and the bowls take the full length.\n\nFOUR PIECES, FOUR SLOTS — deck, bowls, drainer, tap — because a sink cut into a worktop needs its bowl outline separately from its deck outline, and a schedule wants the bowl area on its own.",
